Before test this new package:

	- IT IS ONLY FOR  KERNEL >= 2.6.12
	    See: ftp://ftp.kernel.org/pub/linux/kernel/people/gregkh/driver_core/2.6/2.6.12-rc3/driver-02-2.6.12-rc3.patch
	- IT IS ONLY FOR  KERNEL >= 2.6.9

	- SURE YOU HAVE ACTUAL DRIVER PACKAGE PREPARE TO FULL REINSTALL IT IF
	SOMETHING GO WRONG.
	- DON'T DO ANYTHING IMPORTANT AT COMPUTER WHILE YOU TEST IT.

	- Dowload last version of the package.
	    - cvs -d:pserver:anonymous@cvs.sourceforge.net:/cvsroot/zyxel630-11 login
	    - cvs -z3 -d:pserver:anonymous@cvs.sourceforge.net:/cvsroot/zyxel630-11 co -P amedyn2

	- You need firmware support in kernel, and hotplug.

	    Device Drivers ---->
		Generic Driver Options --->
		    <*> Hotplug firmware loading support

	    General setup ---->
		[*] Support for hot-pluggable devices
		[*] Kernel Userspace Events

	- You need two firmware file, both in:
		- First stage firmware: Init-usb.bin
			You need take it form your Windows drivers. If you don't
			have this file in your Windows system look for the
			correct name at Hardware control panel of the modem.
			¿init-usb.bin?
			Remember save it as Init-usb.bin

		- Second stage firmware: fw-usb.bin or  Fw-usb_A.bin
			If you allready are using the modem you have this file
			in your amdeyn package.
			
		- Copy all this firmware files to /lib/firmware/

		- Copy all this firmware files to /lib/firmware/ and
		    /usr/lib/hotplug/firmware/
		    You need: Init-usb.bin, fw-usb.bin Fw-usb_A.bin
		    
		*** If you use differents names for this files rename its. ***

	- you need hotplug tools:
	    hotplug****.deb, hotplug*****.rpm ...
	    
	    I have hotplug-2004_04_01-8.1.rpm in Fedora Core 3
	    Or hotplug_0.0.20040329-16_all.deb in debian..
	    
	- Uninstal old driver:
		- make remove_service
		- make uninstall

	- Reboot computer. Yes, please reboot it.

	- Install new package:
		- make
		- make install

	- Config /etc/amdyn
		- A new parameter is need, add and set it :
				# Line type
				LINE_TYPE=0x15 # 0x15 = ANALOG, 0x11 = ISDN

	- Try it...
		amstar.sh

	- If it work
		- Say it at forum.
			- Modem
			- kernel version
			- distro (mandrake, fedora core, ...) and version.
			- line type
			- PPPoE/PPPoA/... , 

	- If failed...
		- make uninstall
		- install old version
		- ....go to forum and post...
			- Modem, kernel......
			- amstart.sh output
			- "dmesg" output

Good lucky...

